	(text "J8: 1x10 header, wired to the panel jacks (sheet 4, M8 panel jacks, solder lugs). MIDI IN sleeve has no\nDC path to ground (CA-033); C8 (DNP) is the optional 100 nF RF ground the spec allows.\nTwo jacks are TRS (MIDI), two are TS or TRS with the ring open (audio)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 312.42 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "25bd7632-e9c9-4a7f-a8b2-4eafec42246a")
	)
	(text "SW4 RUN / SW5 BOOT: 6x6 mm tact switches, 4-pin (SW_PUSH_6mm), each to GND.\nThe board sits 6.5 mm behind a 1.6 mm panel, so choose an actuator height of about\n9.5 mm or more (H9.5 / H13 types) to reach through the 4 mm panel holes.\nRUN: module pull-up + C9 on the main board; BOOT: module pad via TP1 on the main board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 171.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7176a0bf-3986-4e95-85bf-9e228a7c9d63")
	)
	(text_box "Front board - 45 x 80 mm, 2 layers, 6.5 mm behind the 10 HP panel\n- Everything the format dictates lives here: SEL encoder with RUN/BOOT beside it, PARAM A/B in a second row, the display on 3.5 mm standoffs,\n  the pull-ups, and the header J8 for the four panel-wired jacks (the jack row sits below the board: panel Y 109.6, board ends at Y 94).\n- Board-to-board: J3/J4 = 2x 1x12 sockets. 19 signals + 3V3 + VSYS + 3x GND = 24. The MIDI current loop crosses; opto and resistors stay on the main board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 218.44 0)
		(size 190.5 19.05)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "be3c96eb-e117-4bfd-8832-e33c0bad291c")
	)
